# Seat: Brand & copy — round 7 working notes

Build: commit 984a0f17 (frozen). Driving `_gate-suite.html` in chromium.
Written as I go.

## Sweep 1 — static strings, tasks.board / notes.notebook / timeline.owner-flight @1440

Register overall: calm, declarative, sentence case, no exclamation marks, no
jargon. Eyebrows are mono uppercase and consistently used. Counts reconcile
(8 to decide = 1+1+3+2+1; 14 notes = 3+1+5+3+2; 5 of 13 done).

CANDIDATE A — "One thing is not going ahead." (Timeline, behind-you note,
master.html:21455). The product's noun for its own object is "moment"
("Add a moment", "3 moments", "What is still ahead"). In exactly one
sentence — the one the OWNER reads — it becomes "thing". And the guest
branch (21457-21461) names the cancelled moment outright ("The city hotel
shortlist is not going ahead."), so the owner is given LESS than the guest
about her own plan. Two grammars for one fact, and the vaguer one is
pointed at the person who can act.

CANDIDATE B — date grammar inside one region. `b-behindDate` renders
"Sat 18 Apr" (weekdayShort + short) while the summary sentence directly
above it renders the same class of fact as "18 April" (fmt.medium),
and reads "the last of them 18 April" with no preposition.

## Sweep 2 — driving the seam (notebook -> lift -> select -> peel -> send -> open)

CANDIDATE C (strong) — the seam protests too much, and never says where the
card landed. Driving one crossing produces, in order:
  1 .peelBoundary  "Your note stays here. Tasks only ever receives the exact
                    words you pick and check below."
  2 live (peel)    "Tasks receives these words and nothing else from this note.
                    The rest of what you wrote stays private here."
  3 .peelWhy       "Your note is still here, still private, still yours to edit."
  4 live (send)    "Sent to Tasks. Your note stayed here. In The house."
  5 live (open)    "Opened in Tasks. Your note stayed in Notes."
  (+ posed notes.seam fixture, .cnt: "3 so far, and every note stayed here")
Five wordings of one promise in one gesture; the tense wanders stays ->
stays private -> is still here -> stayed here -> stayed in Notes; and #3 is
the only string in the suite that reaches for rhetoric (triple anaphora).
Meanwhile the card lands in **To do** and NOTHING says so in words: not the
receipt, not the send announcement, not the arrival announcement. #5 spends
its second sentence on a fourth repetition of the promise instead of the one
fact the person does not already know.

CANDIDATE D — the seam carries Notes' vocabulary into Tasks unchanged.
Notes files under "The house / The studio / The course / The enquiries".
Tasks tags read "Venue / Bar / Enquiry". Send a note filed under "The house"
and the card arrives tagged "The house", standing beside "Venue" and "Bar".
"The enquiries" (Notes) and "Enquiry" (Tasks) are the same bucket under two
names, in the one product whose argument is that there is one world under
all three.

## Sweep 3 — the honest doors (driven, not read)

FINDING (confirmed, hard) — **the More door announces the opposite of what
it did.** Press More on the spine: `.morePop` opens (aria-expanded="true",
"Also in Signal Studio / Home / Inbox / Help", each "Not here yet"), and the
live region says **"More, closed."** Press again: the menu closes
(aria-expanded="false") and the live region says **"More, open."**
Cause: master.html:11443 calls `say(moreOpen ? "More, open." : "More, closed.")`
OUTSIDE the morph callback, so it reads the pre-toggle value. The sibling
control does it right — Projects (14990) calls say() INSIDE the callback,
after `projOpen = !projOpen`, and announces correctly.
The doors are the brief's designed answer to what is not built; this one
tells a screen-reader user the reverse of the truth, every press, in both
directions. Reproduced from notes.notebook, dispatched click and Enter.

ALSO — the privacy door inverts the doors' declared grammar. Every other
door is "name the thing. Not here yet. [one sentence]":
  "Your account, in Signal Studio. Not here yet."
  "Every project in one list. Not here yet."
  "A photo, read into words. Not here yet."
The privacy door answers "Yours until you send something on. Your privacy
settings. Not here yet." — the name arrives second, and the first sentence
is a verbatim repeat of the second half of the button's own accessible name
("Private to you. Yours until you send something on."), which the reader
heard one keystroke earlier. Source: master.html:19716.
And it is the ONE door with no visible answer: options, photo and the
account tile all paint a visible "Not here yet"; privacy answers only in
the live region.

ALSO — the Notes head "…" is two names for one door: accessible name
"Notes options" (product scope), answer "More for this note. Not here yet."
(one-note scope) — and in notes.notebook at rest no note is open at all;
the desk is an empty capture field. The source comment at 19712 justifies
the string by a button called "More actions for this note" that does not
exist in the suite.

## Sweep 4 — naming collisions (driven)

FINDING (confirmed) — **two controls named "More" on one phone screen.**
timeline.owner-flight @390: `.b-more` (the head's "···", y=140) and
`.railTile[More]` (the dock, y=783) both carry aria-label "More" and
aria-haspopup="menu". The first opens a menu ALSO labelled "More" holding
Preview / Get the link — this plan's sharing. The second opens "Also in
Signal Studio: Home / Inbox / Help / Settings" — the rest of the suite.
Two unrelated destinations, one name, 643px apart, only at <=720 where the
head collapses its acts. At 1440 the head spells them out and the collision
disappears, which is why frames hide it.

OBSERVED — the identity tile is printed twice at desk width (spine
`.railAvatar` + product `.dockAvatar`, both "OR", both titled "Your account,
in Signal Studio. Not here yet.") and carries TWO accessible names:
"Orla, venue manager" everywhere except Notes' dock tile, which is
"Orla, venue manager. Not here yet.".

FINDING (confirmed) — **the dictation floor's privacy claim is about
typing.** master.html:9410, rendered only at 18684, i.e. only on the
dictation floor: "Signal Studio keeps the words, not the audio. Typing
stays on this device until you save." Nobody types on that screen. The
first sentence tells her the words are kept by Signal Studio; the second,
which is the one that should say what happens to what she just SAID before
she saves, is about a different verb. Two sentences, and the one that
matters answers the wrong question.

## Sweep 5 — checks that came back clean (recorded so no one re-runs them)

- Counts reconcile under driving, not just in the frames: "8 to decide" =
  1+1+3+2+1 group tails; "14 notes" = 14 rows; "5 of 13 done / 38%" becomes
  "5 of 14 / 36%" the instant a note crosses the seam and "8 to decide"
  becomes "7"; the dense fold says exactly the number of cards whose box is
  outside the scroller, correct at 1920, 1440 and 1280 in all five lanes.
  (I mis-read the To do fold off the frame and the measurement refuted me.)
- The filter is the model of what the seam should be: "Showing 1 overdue
  task. 12 others are hidden." is one string in one grammar, printed AND
  announced, and released with "Showing all work."
- Empty search: "Nothing matches." on screen, "No task says "marqueezzzz"."
  aloud — different, but the announcement adds the query, so it earns it.
- Register holds everywhere: sentence case, no exclamation marks, no
  jargon, no marketing voice. Eyebrows are consistently noun phrases.
  Task titles carry no terminal stop; card notes and lane notes do; the
  peel strips the note's full stop when the words become a title. That is
  a real rule, kept.
- The five lane notes ("Agreed and ready to start." / "In motion right now."
  / "Being checked before it goes out." / "Held by a reply, a delivery, or a
  decision." / "Finished and put away.") teach the board without a tooltip.
- "Timeline is another surface in this suite. This lab is the Notes one."
  (master.html:19700) is a LAB leak, but no control in the suite carries
  data-act="timeline", so it is unreachable. Not reported.
- voiceStop: "Stop listening" (9406) is dead — the markup hardcodes
  "Stop and read it back". Not reported.
- Timeline's owner behind-note says "One thing is not going ahead." where
  the guest's names the moment. Noun drift (moment -> thing) and the owner
  gets less than the guest. Real, but a refuter can argue the owner already
  knows which one, so it did not make the five.
- The account tile prints twice at desk width (spine + dock) with two
  accessible names. Real, small, did not make the five.

## Score

9.1. The copy is genuinely in Linear/Stripe territory for tone and for
arithmetic honesty. What holds it off 9.5 is five string-level defects, two
of which actively mislead: the More door announces the reverse of what it
did, and the dictation floor's privacy sentence answers about typing. One
door answers a sighted person with nothing. Two buttons share one name on
the phone. And the seam — the gesture the whole suite exists to justify —
spends its entire copy budget reassuring and never names the lane it chose.
All five are strings or one-liners; none is a build and none is a different
decision. Roughly a day.
